---
import type { ImageMetadata } from 'astro';
import { Image, getImage } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

// Drop a square photo at src/assets/portrait.jpg (or .png/.webp) and it
// shows up here automatically; delete the file to go back to text-only.
const portraitFiles = import.meta.glob<{ default: ImageMetadata }>(
  '../assets/portrait.{jpg,jpeg,png,webp}',
  { eager: true },
);
const portrait = Object.values(portraitFiles)[0]?.default;

// Point JSON-LD at an optimized rendition rather than portrait.src, so the
// full-size original never ships in the build.
const portraitJsonLdImage = portrait
  ? await getImage({ src: portrait, width: 800, format: 'webp' })
  : undefined;

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Person',
  name: 'Justin Soderstrom',
  url: 'https://justinsoderstrom.com',
  jobTitle: 'Lead Software Engineer',
  ...(portraitJsonLdImage && {
    image: new URL(portraitJsonLdImage.src, Astro.site).href,
  }),
  sameAs: [
    'https://github.com/justinsoderstrom',
    'https://www.linkedin.com/in/justinsoderstrom/',
  ],
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Justin Soderstrom: Lead Software Engineer"
  description="Justin Soderstrom is a Lead Software Engineer designing and delivering cloud-native .NET systems on Azure. Projects, resume, and writing on software development."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <section class="hero">
    {
      portrait && (
        <Image
          src={portrait}
          alt="Portrait of Justin Soderstrom"
          width={112}
          densities={[1, 2]}
          class="hero-portrait"
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
        />
      )
    }
    <div>
      <h1>Hi, I'm Justin.</h1>
      <p class="tagline">Lead Software Engineer</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <p>
    I'm a Lead Software Engineer at CCC Intelligent Solutions with nearly a
    decade of experience designing, building, and operating cloud-native .NET
    systems on Azure. Most of that time has gone into ASP.NET Core APIs and
    microservices behind business-critical products, including eight services at
    CCC that together handle around 45 million requests a month, with full-stack
    web and desktop work when the problem called for it.
  </p>

  <p>
    These days, I'm leading a team of four other engineers modernizing specific
    modules of CCC ONE: moving functionality from the legacy desktop product
    onto web APIs, and building new microservices where they fit. CCC ONE is
    used by roughly 30,000 repair shops, so each module moves over with full
    backward compatibility while every shop keeps running. That's the kind of
    work I do best: hard technical problems I can own end to end, from system
    design through production.
  </p>

  <p>
    While my background is in C#, most of my code now comes from AI agents I
    direct and review, primarily using Claude Code. The architecture, the
    trade-offs, and the call on what ships stay with me; the agents handle more
    of the typing. In fact, this entire website was built the same way, and <a
      href="https://github.com/justinsoderstrom/justinsoderstrom.github.io"
      >the code is on GitHub</a
    >!
  </p>

  <p>
    Outside of work, I live in Grand Rapids, Michigan with my wife and child. I
    love to read, hike, play games, and spend time with my family.
  </p>

  <p>
    Have a look at my <a href="/projects/">projects</a>, skim my <a
      href="/resume/">resume</a
    >, or read the <a href="/blog/">blog</a>, where I occasionally write about
    software development. If you're hiring for your team, I'd love to <a
      href="/contact/">hear from you</a
    >!
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
